# The reviewing half: an agent's branch of polar, three files. c walks the hunks; the new endpoint
# calls a new service method, d opens it, and right under it sits get_or_raise_by_key, a name one
# swap away. u shows who calls that one: the customer portal, and Enter opens a portal endpoint
# that needs no authentication, while the new method checks the caller's organizations. One c
# brings the review back; the refactored endpoints and the tests are walked to the end.
project polar
merl --review
wait hunk 1/9
sleep 0.5
show
sleep 1.8

# c: the imports the refactor dropped, then the new endpoint, read whole
key c
wait hunk 2/9
sleep 0.9
key c
wait hunk 3/9
sleep 2.6

# the endpoint calls a service method the branch adds: / onto it, Esc clears the find, d
key /
sleep 0.2
type@0.08 get_by
sleep 0.4
key Enter
sleep 0.5
key Escape
sleep 0.3
key d
wait LicenseKeyService.get_by_key_or_raise
sleep 2.2

# Ctrl+D reads on: right under the new method, a namesake
key C-d
sleep 2.4

# u on the namesake: the customer portal calls it; Enter opens one of its endpoints
key /
sleep 0.2
type@0.08 get_or
sleep 0.4
key Enter
sleep 0.4
key u
wait Usages of get_or_raise_by_key
sleep 2.2
key Down Down
sleep 0.4
key Enter
wait customer_portal/endpoints/license_keys.py
sleep 3.2

# c: back to the review where it stood, then on through validate, activate and deactivate
key c
wait hunk 3/9
sleep 0.9
key c
wait hunk 4/9
sleep 1.6
key c
wait hunk 5/9
sleep 0.7
key c
wait hunk 6/9
sleep 1.0
key c
wait hunk 7/9
sleep 0.6
key c
wait hunk 8/9
sleep 0.9
key c
wait hunk 9/9
sleep 0.6

# c: the service file, already read on the way; c: the tests, read whole with Ctrl+D
key c
wait file 2/3
sleep 1.0
key c
wait file 3/3
sleep 1.0
key C-d
sleep 2.4
key C-d
sleep 2.6
key c
wait last hunk of the review
sleep 2.4
